#
# Counter-example for math:GramMatrixShape: a math:GramMatrix whose entry at (0, 1)
# carries 1/4 but whose transpose entry at (1, 0) carries 1/2 — no transpose entry of
# equal value, so the matrix is not symmetric. It names its math:representsForm
# (a math:SymmetricBilinearForm) and math:inBasis (a math:Basis), and every entry's
# math:RationalValue is well-formed, so ONLY the sh:sparql symmetry constraint fires.
# Validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and no other finding
# (math:AsymmetricGramMatrix).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecGramMatrixAsymmetric).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:asymGram a math:GramMatrix ;
    math:representsForm ex:asymForm ;
    math:inBasis ex:asymBasis ;
    math:hasEntry ex:a01 , ex:a10 .

ex:asymForm a math:SymmetricBilinearForm .
ex:asymBasis a math:Basis .

ex:a01 a math:MatrixEntry ; math:atRow 0 ; math:atColumn 1 ; math:entryValue ex:rQuarter .
ex:a10 a math:MatrixEntry ; math:atRow 1 ; math:atColumn 0 ; math:entryValue ex:rHalf .

ex:rQuarter a math:RationalValue ; math:numerator 1 ; math:denominator 4 .
ex:rHalf a math:RationalValue ; math:numerator 1 ; math:denominator 2 .
